1. PURPOSE AND REPOSITORY ROLE

This license applies to the factory-managed public commercial surface of CHLOM™, the Compliance Hybrid Licensing and Ownership Model. The repository is published for discovery, documentation, interoperability evaluation, research orientation, public-safe verification, developer onboarding, licensing inquiry, and authorized commercial integration.

Public visibility is not an open-source, open-content, patent, trademark, data, model-training, production, certification, or commercial-use grant.

2. REPOSITORY FAMILY

The canonical governance parent is `crownthrive1/CrownThrive-OS`. It controls the managed public policy and commercial projection package for CHLOM.

The public commercial child is `crownthrive/chlom-protocol`. It carries public-safe architecture, registries, schemas, research, integration surfaces, documentation, and factory-managed commercial material.

Both repositories are public. Restricted source material, secrets, protected evidence, private contracts, confidential implementation logic, private economic logic, protected-person data, and other non-public state are not authorized for publication in either repository.

A parent or child commit does not create rights outside the authority and evidence actually attached to that record.

