6. DAIL, DLA, IDENTITY, AND FINGERPRINTS

DAIL means Decentralized Autonomous Information Ledger. DLA means Dynamic Licensing Asset.

Public identifiers, DIDs, hashes, fingerprints, provenance references, signatures, attestations, and ledger records are evidence-bearing technical records. They do not automatically prove ownership, authorship, legal validity, exclusivity, identity, or enforceability without the controlling rights and evidence context.

No permission is granted to clone, reconstruct, spoof, forge, or misrepresent CrownThrive identifiers, certification marks, fingerprints, issuer authority, or rights records.

